  vignette: "A 24-year-old man has 3.8 extracted uneventfully; bleeding stops with pressure before he leaves. Six hours later he returns with a steadily bleeding socket. He reports prolonged bleeding after a childhood circumcision and that a maternal uncle 'has a blood problem'. Platelet count is normal. The most likely diagnosis is:",
